Quoting  L <L_1_L_0@yahoo.com>:
>The problem with completing NetHack unspoiled is that the major
>Oracular consulations do NOT tell you either of these things:
>* How to get holy water.

But the Guidebook strongly hints at one method;

Clear  potions  are  potions  of water.  Sometimes these are
blessed or cursed, resulting in holy or unholy water.  Holy water
is  the  bane  of  the  undead, so potions of holy water are good
things to throw (`t') at them.  It is also sometimes very useful
to dip (``#dip'') an object into a potion.

>* Armor that sufficiently covers the body might be able to block magic
>(i.e magic cancellation.)

I really don't see the latter as a problem at all. Almost any set of
armour assembled with a view to its other properties will have MC 2 or 3.
It is quite feasible to ascend with MC 2.

>Has anyone ever ascended with _no_ magic cancellation at all?

I don't see the problem with this being the lack of MC but the difficulty
of doing without a cloak. Sure, it's not impossible, but I think that's
more pain than having to deal with leveldrainers.
